WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.150
Two things make the gates trustworthy.

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.374
First, every gate criterion
is evaluated from the

3
00:00:05.374 --> 00:00:08.913
repository and the drift
reports, not from a signature.

4
00:00:08.913 --> 00:00:14.012
Zero drift for fourteen days is a
query; so is every PC cloud-joined.

5
00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:16.924
The engine reports green,
the steward concurs,

6
00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:20.525
and the record that merges the
decision shows who made it.

7
00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:23.950
A gate the engine can't evaluate
needs a better criterion.

8
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.785
Second, rollback triggers are thresholds,

9
00:00:26.785 --> 00:00:30.512
not judgment calls, and the
values are the agency's to set.

10
00:00:30.512 --> 00:00:34.137
Drift above the threshold for
more than a day halts the phase.

11
00:00:34.137 --> 00:00:37.337
Conditional Access blocking
more than a set share

12
00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:40.613
of legitimate sign-ins means
the policy is reverted.

13
00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:44.437
If drift detection stops
reporting, all phase work halts.

14
00:00:44.437 --> 00:00:46.601
Authority is fixed in advance.

15
00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:50.525
The steward clears G0, G1 and G4.

16
00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:53.337
The steward and the sponsor co-sign G2.

17
00:00:53.337 --> 00:00:56.637
The sponsor and the steering
committee clear G3.

18
00:00:56.637 --> 00:01:01.651
And the sponsor and the CIO clear
G5, Active Directory retired.

19
00:01:01.651 --> 00:01:03.237
And be clear about the end.

20
00:01:03.237 --> 00:01:06.544
A forest in backup isn't
a lasting fallback:

21
00:01:06.544 --> 00:01:12.212
a backup is valid only within the
tombstone lifetime, 180 days by default.

22
00:01:12.212 --> 00:01:16.700
The real rollback point is the last
moment a domain controller still runs.

23
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.701
So G5 is the sponsor's and the
CIO's decision, made on evidence:

24
00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:25.356
no live production dependency on
Active Directory authentication,

25
00:01:25.356 --> 00:01:29.180
or a documented Kerberos island
with an end-of-life date.
